@meta
id: 16-10
title: A file the list does not have
chapter: 16
type: lesson
skills: split-window, window-nav
par: 95
minutes: 5
vscode: Ctrl-P, changelog, Enter, and it opens over the file you were reading
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
So far every file you have touched was opened for you. The ticket for
the refund window has landed in the provider and the reviewer wants a
line in `CHANGELOG.md`, which is not open and is not in the list. `:sp`
takes a filename: `:sp CHANGELOG.md` opens that file in a new window
above the current one, and the provider stays exactly where it was
below. If the name does not exist yet, the window opens empty and the
file is created when you write it.

Under `## Unreleased`, below the existing bullet, add:

    - 30 day refund window on cancellation (ORD-418)

The provider is open for you to check the ticket number against the
code; it does not change.

@keys
| `:sp name` | open `name` in a new window above this one |
| `:new name` | the same thing; `:new` alone opens an empty scratch window |
| `Ctrl-W n` | `:new` as a chord |
| `Ctrl-W j` `Ctrl-W k` | down a window, up a window |

@hints
`:sp CHANGELOG.md`. The cursor is in the new window, on line 1 of the
changelog.
--
`/reason` lands on the existing bullet. `o`, the new bullet, `Esc`.
--
`:wqa` writes the changelog and closes both windows. Nothing was
changed in the provider, so it is not written.

@solution
    :sp CHANGELOG.md<Enter>  /reason<Enter>  o - 30 day refund window on cancellation (ORD-418) <Esc>  :wqa<Enter>

Around eighty keystrokes, fifty of them the bullet.

Until chapter 18 gives you `:e` and `:find`, `:sp name` is your way of
opening a file that nobody opened for you, and it is often the better
way even afterwards: the file you were in does not go anywhere, and
the new one is a window away rather than a buffer away. Chapter 18's
finding tools all have a split form for exactly that reason.

`:new` with no name is the scratch pad: an empty window for a draft
commit message, a list of ids to work through, a bit of code you want
to reshape before pasting it back. `:q!` throws it away; `:w name`
keeps it.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    // ORD-418: refunds only inside the 30 day window
    const days = (Date.now() - order.placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;

    if (days <= 30) {
      await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

      return this.orderRepository.update({
        where: { id },
        values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
      });
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED', cancellationReason: 'REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED' },
    });
  }
}

@start CHANGELOG.md
# Changelog

## Unreleased

- cancellation records a reason (ORD-402)

## 1.4.0

- customer lookup by email
- refunds go through the payment service
- order status SHIPPED

@expected CHANGELOG.md
# Changelog

## Unreleased

- cancellation records a reason (ORD-402)
- 30 day refund window on cancellation (ORD-418)

## 1.4.0

- customer lookup by email
- refunds go through the payment service
- order status SHIPPED
